1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,500
Leather jacket.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,500
Three point four trillion dollars.

3
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,000
Jensen Huang built NVIDIA into
the world's most valuable company.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,500
Then he blew it up.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
First, he was caught with Alice Huang,
a Chinese executive

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,500
U.S. intelligence says was a spy.

7
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,500
Then, a second affair, with his own VP
who reported to him.

8
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:21,000
On November twelfth, after thirty three
years as CEO, Jensen resigned.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,500
Effective immediately.

10
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,000
The board didn't even fight it.

11
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:28,500
NVIDIA stock crashed
fourteen percent at the open.

12
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,500
It recovered to close down four percent,
but the real damage?

13
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:35,000
One point six trillion dollars in
market value, wiped out over six weeks.

14
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
That's bigger than the
entire GDP of Australia.

15
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,500
AMD surged thirty percent this week.

16
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,000
Broadcom jumped twenty four percent.

17
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,500
But NVIDIA's partners got crushed.

18
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:51,500
CoreWeave dropped seven percent,
and TSMC fell with it.

19
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Analysts now value NVIDIA at
two twenty five per share without Jensen,

20
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,500
down from three hundred.

21
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:02,000
The new interim CEO, Colette Kress,
is a finance executive, not an engineer.

22
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,500
And NVIDIA's earnings drop
November seventeenth.

23
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:08,500
Can anyone replace the man
in the leather jacket?

24
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:12,000
The bull case. NVIDIA is now at its
cheapest valuation in years,

25
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,000
and AI demand isn't slowing.

26
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,500
The bear case. No successor,
a spy scandal, and Congress wants answers.

27
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:20,000
This is not financial advice.

28
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:23,000
Follow for more finance breakdowns.

29
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,500
Drop a comment, who should be
NVIDIA's next CEO?
